  "title": "fix(tdmpc): advance CEM warm starts by the executed action chunk",
  "body": "## Summary / Motivation\n\nWhen `n_action_steps > 1`, `select_action` consumes that many distinct actions before planning again, but CEM always shifts the previous mean by one. For a five-step plan with three executed actions, the next initialization retains `[m1, m2, m3, m4, 0]` instead of the unexecuted tail `[m3, m4, 0, 0, 0]`. With finite CEM iterations this can change the next selected action.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Shift the previous mean by `n_action_steps`, leaving the newly exposed tail at zero.\n- Keep the default one-step behavior, repeated-single-action behavior, and reset semantics.\n- Add 16 CPU cases through real `select_action -> predict_action_chunk -> plan` calls, including batch sizes 1/2, chunk lengths 1/2/3/5, a fully consumed horizon, repeated actions, and reset.\n\n## How was this tested\n\nThe tests control only CEM's Gaussian proposals; the action queue, planner, latent dynamics and value networks run normally. On unmodified main, the six multi-action cases fail and ten controls pass. With this change, all 16 pass.\n\nPython 3.12.13, PyTorch 2.15.0, CPU. Exact commit: `69747d8f44403ac64c6f15bdb1429df8150de4f0`.\n\n| Fork Fast Tests tier | Passed | Skipped |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Base | 2,585 | 540 |\n| Dataset | 1,757 | 132 |\n| Hardware | 7 | 72 |\n| Visualization | 9 | 151 |\n\n[Baseline](https://github.com/Afloat16/lerobot/actions/runs/43961818735) · [Final tests](https://github.com/Afloat16/lerobot/actions/runs/43963629106) · [Quality](https://github.com/Afloat16/lerobot/actions/runs/43963629165)\n\nThe Quality run passed after retrying a Go dependency download failure. To reproduce the focused check:\n\n```bash\nuv sync --locked --extra test\nuv run pytest tests/policies/tdmpc/test_warm_start.py -q\n```\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Linting/formatting: all pre-commit hooks passed in fork CI.\n- [ ] All tests pass locally: verification was executed in fork CI.\n- [x] Documentation updated: warm-start comment.\n- [ ] CI is green: upstream PR checks are pending.\n- [ ] Community Review: review of #4692 is prepared; posting is pending.\n\n## Reviewer notes\n\nThe repeat path uses one planned action multiple times and retains its existing one-step shift. This change adds no parameters or checkpoint fields. The regression establishes correct warm-start alignment; it does not measure trained-policy success rates.\n\nAI assistance: ChatGPT assisted with implementation and regression tests.",
  "prefilled_url": "https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/compare/main...Afloat16:lerobot:fix/tdmpc-action-chunk-warm-start-20261116?expand=1&title=fix(tdmpc)%3A%20advance%20CEM%20warm%20starts%20by%20the%20executed%20action%20chunk&body=%23%23%20Summary%20%2F%20Motivation%0A%0AWhen%20%60n_action_steps%20%3E%201%60%2C%20%60select_action%60%20consumes%20that%20many%20distinct%20actions%20before%20planning%20again%2C%20but%20CEM%20always%20shifts%20the%20previous%20mean%20by%20one.%20For%20a%20five-step%20plan%20with%20three%20executed%20actions%2C%20the%20next%20initialization%20retains%20%60%5Bm1%2C%20m2%2C%20m3%2C%20m4%2C%200%5D%60%20instead%20of%20the%20unexecuted%20tail%20%60%5Bm3%2C%20m4%2C%200%2C%200%2C%200%5D%60.%20With%20finite%20CEM%20iterations%20this%20can%20change%20the%20next%20selected%20action.%0A%0A%23%23%20What%20changed%0A%0A-%20Shift%20the%20previous%20mean%20by%20%60n_action_steps%60%2C%20leaving%20the%20newly%20exposed%20tail%20at%20zero.%0A-%20Keep%20the%20default%20one-step%20behavior%2C%20repeated-single-action%20behavior%2C%20and%20reset%20semantics.%0A-%20Add%2016%20CPU%20cases%20through%20real%20%60select_action%20-%3E%20predict_action_chunk%20-%3E%20plan%60%20calls%2C%20including%20batch%20sizes%201%2F2%2C%20chunk%20lengths%201%2F2%2F3%2F5%2C%20a%20fully%20consumed%20horizon%2C%20repeated%20actions%2C%20and%20reset.%0A%0A%23%23%20How%20was%20this%20tested%0A%0AThe%20tests%20control%20only%20CEM's%20Gaussian%20proposals%3B%20the%20action%20queue%2C%20planner%2C%20latent%20dynamics%20and%20value%20networks%20run%20normally.%20On%20unmodified%20main%2C%20the%20six%20multi-action%20cases%20fail%20and%20ten%20controls%20pass.%20With%20this%20change%2C%20all%2016%20pass.%0A%0APython%203.12.13%2C%20PyTorch%202.15.0%2C%20CPU.%20Exact%20commit%3A%20%6069747d8f44403ac64c6f15bdb1429df8150de4f0%60.%0A%0A%7C%20Fork%20Fast%20Tests%20tier%20%7C%20Passed%20%7C%20Skipped%20%7C%0A%7C%20---%20%7C%20---%3A%20%7C%20---%3A%20%7C%0A%7C%20Base%20%7C%202%2C585%20